# Toy Audio Agent

Basic steps to run the toy demo locally.

## Requirements

- [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/)

`uv` is the only required tool for local setup. It will manage the project Python environment for you.

Install `uv` if you do not already have it:

```bash
curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
```

## Before You Start

This demo expects audio `.wav` files under the path set by `AUDIO_DIR`.

The app reads these environment variables:

```bash
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
AUDIO_DIR=<path_to_folder_with_audio>
```

The app also loads a local `.env` file automatically.

If not set, it falls back to:

```bash
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
AUDIO_DIR=audio/
```

## Ollama

You need access to an Ollama server.

You can use either:

- a local Ollama server, usually at `http://localhost:11434`
- a remote Ollama server, using its reachable host URL

If you are using a remote server, set `OLLAMA_HOST` to the correct hostname before starting the app.

The demo uses the `qwen3-vl:latest` model.

If you are running Ollama locally, install it from [`ollama.com`](https://ollama.com/) and pull the model with:

```bash
ollama pull qwen3-vl:latest
```

## Setup

Create the local virtual environment and install dependencies:

```bash
uv sync
```

This creates `.venv/` for the project automatically.

Run project commands with `uv run <command>`.

Create a local `.env` file before starting the app:

```bash
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
AUDIO_DIR=<path_to_folder_with_audio>
```

Or export the same values in your shell:

```bash
export OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
export AUDIO_DIR=<path_to_folder_with_audio>
```

## Run The Demo

Start the app with:

```bash
uv run uvicorn main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 7932 --reload --reload-include main.py
```

Then open:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:7932
```

## Notes

- `list_audio_files()` only looks for `.wav` files in `AUDIO_DIR`.
- `generate_spectrogram()` reads files relative to `AUDIO_DIR` and returns a generated spectrogram image.
